      "hints": [
        "Combine fractions over $\\cos\\theta(1+\\sin\\theta)$.",
        "Use $\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1$ in numerator to get $2 + 2\\sin\\theta$.",
        "Factor out $2$ and cancel $(1+\\sin\\theta)$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Combine the fractions over the common denominator $\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta)$:\n$$\\frac{1 + \\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta} + \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{1 + \\sin\\theta} = \\frac{(1 + \\sin\\theta)^2 + \\cos^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta)}$$",
        "Expand the numerator:\n$$= \\frac{1 + 2\\sin\\theta + \\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta)}$$",
        "Apply the Pythagorean identity $\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1$ in the numerator:\n$$= \\frac{1 + 2\\sin\\theta + 1}{\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta)} = \\frac{2 + 2\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta)}$$",
        "Factor out $2$ in the numerator and cancel the common factor $(1 + \\sin\\theta)$:\n$$= \\frac{2(1 + \\sin\\theta)}{\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta)} = \\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Trigonometric Identities": "Combines over common denominator (M1). Uses $\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta=1$ (M1). Factorises and cancels to obtain $\\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta}$ (A1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
