      "hints": [
        "Replace LHS with $\\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta}$ to get $\\tan\\theta = 1.5$.",
        "Find solutions in radians on $[0, 2\\pi]$ to $3$ significant figures."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Replace the left-hand side with the identity $\\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta}$:\n$$\\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta} = \\frac{3}{\\sin\\theta}$$",
        "Rearrange into terms of $\\tan\\theta$:\n$$2\\sin\\theta = 3\\cos\\theta \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\frac{3}{2} = 1.5$$",
        "Find both solutions in radians on the interval $0 \\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi$:\n$$\\theta = \\tan^{-1}(1.5) \\approx 0.983\\text{ rad}$$\n$$\\theta = 0.9828 + \\pi \\approx 4.12\\text{ rad}$$"
      ],
